            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0246" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20210/2011: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-04T21:00:00-03:00">November 4, 1942—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2178. Embassy’s 2169, November 3, 9 p.m. Minister of Foreign Affairs informed me
                    tonight memorandum handed to Ministry of the Interior 11 o’clock last night.
                    Chief of Police<anchor n="73" xml:id="d216-f1"/> who has taken entire charge has
                    already found very interesting confirmation in first investigations made.
                    Minister expressed hope that every opportunity may be given him without
                    publicity to complete investigations which they promise will be prosecuted
                    vigorously and effectively.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d216-f1" n="73" xml:id="d216-f1-content">
